## A-item verification

- A3: the checker counts rows with a labeled line count (`grep -c
  'scenes/maps/'`) compared by integer arithmetic (`-eq 30`, `-ge 1`), and every
  cell parse is labeled (`MAPS rating:`, `MAPS note:`, `maker:`, state cell
  `$(NF-1)`). No bare digit match decides a count or a bound.
- A4: an absent or empty inventory fails P1-a (red-p1.log records exit 1 with
  `FAIL: P1-a inventory file absent`). The phase holds 2 completed `[x]` tasks,
  so a markers-consistent pass is not vacuous.
- A5: every plan claim was re-verified. Red exited 1 before the inventory existed
  (8e20f73d, red-p1.log lines 6 to 10). The checker exits 0 with the exact quoted
  Total line. The plan gate prints 30. 30 rows exist; the checker's P1-b proves
  the 150 named paths exist; every row holds MAPS rating 7.0, a source note,
  `judge: no`, `maker: Anthropic Sonnet`, and state `inventoried`; no row is
  `missing`. The e964238a fixes named in the plan are present in the committed
  checker.
- A6: the registry entry in `measure/tracks.md` at 3e8d29e8 reads `[~] Track:
  Plan and accept civic scenes`; plan.md status reads `in_progress`. No
  completion claim precedes this acceptance.
- A7: the slug set comes from all 30 civic P2 TSV rows via awk
  (`$2=="civic" && $3=="P2"`). No filter drops a slug. No banned-term filter
  masks a hit: probe ADV-P1-08 shows a claude-family judge claim still fails
  P1-c.

## Independent fidelity check

An awk loop took the final `bench/sonnet/log.tsv` row per civic slug (score
field 11, note field 13; an empty note reads `none recorded`) and compared all
30 rows with the inventory cells. No mismatch line printed: 30 of 30 agree. This
confirms the record independently of the checker's pinned table and of the
prior reviews.

## Review currency decision

Reviews A and C at feeca3f3 still cover Phase 1. They must not run again.

Reason: the implementation content of the phase is byte-identical at HEAD.
`scenes/inventory.md` was last changed at db233e01 and `plan.md` at 2e8e4f01,
both before feeca3f3. Every commit after feeca3f3 (0355d23c, 54213a00, 3e8d29e8)
touches only test files under `measure/runs/`. The one reviewed test file that
changed, `check-inventory.sh` at 54213a00, is the remediation of the Review A and
Review C nits; the adversarial re-audit PASS at 54213a00 covers it, and this
acceptance re-ran both gates live at HEAD. The test-only-commit rule applies.
This acceptance records the exact HEAD 3e8d29e8 and names the allowed test-only
commits: 0355d23c, 54213a00, 3e8d29e8.

## UX browser review decision

The UX browser review does not apply to Phase 1.

Reason: the phase diff adds records only. It touches no shot, scene source,
mockup JPG, page, route, or app path. The 30 three-quarter and top shots are
inputs that Phase 1 does not modify, so a browser look can falsify no Phase 1
claim. Test strategy section 9 ties the judge rating and the human look at the
images to the closing of Phase 2 and Phase 3, and section 10 routes the visual
look of the 30 shots to the Phase 2 judge. Review C recorded the same decision
(`ux_applicability: not_applicable`). The browser review becomes due when
Phase 2 rates the shots or Phase 3 produces fresh rework shots.

## Carried finding

ADV-5 from adversarial-54213a0.json stays a Nit for later phases: the checker
pins the expected MAPS values inside `maps_expected`
(check-inventory.sh:37-71) instead of parsing `bench/sonnet/log.tsv` live. The
pinned table equals the live log today (this audit compared all 30 rows). A later
phase that regenerates the log or `docs/map-review.html` must re-diff the pinned
table against the live file.

## Result

Phase 1 "Inventory" passes acceptance at 3e8d29e8. Blocking findings: none.
Nonblocking findings: the carried ADV-5 Nit above. Retry recommendation: none.

